# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# The Deskbar preferences carry the text size: two clicks and the whole
# interface reads bigger, proven by the leaf menu growing taller.
wait 12
click 980 20
wait 2
note at 12 px the leaf menu ends at 206, above the point below --
note probed clear of the arrow column, since this is about the HEIGHT
expect-pixel 700 215 336698
menu-pick Settings
wait 3
menu-pick Deskbar preferences
wait 5
note the PLUS, which is now a button a press can land on: the row used
note to be the string "-  12 px  +" split at a written-down pixel, and
note which half a click fell in moved with the face and the number
click 715 270
wait 3
key w ctrl
wait 3
click 980 20
wait 3
note at 14 px the same rows reach past it: the menu ran to 206,
note and now runs to 224 -- taller rows, the same number of them
expect-pixel 700 215 d8d8d8
quit
